@module flutter-m10 | Firebase
@summary Add authentication, Firestore, storage, messaging, Crashlytics and analytics with Firebase.

@lesson flutter-m10-l01 | Firebase setup | 8
## Learning objectives
- Connect a Flutter app to Firebase

## Firebase setup
Install the Firebase CLI and FlutterFire CLI, run `flutterfire configure` to generate `firebase_options.dart`, then initialise Firebase before runApp.

```dart
import 'package:firebase_core/firebase_core.dart';
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';
// import 'firebase_options.dart';

Future<void> main() async {
  WidgetsFlutterBinding.ensureInitialized();
  await Firebase.initializeApp(/* options: DefaultFirebaseOptions.currentPlatform */);
  runApp(const MaterialApp(home: Text('Ready')));
}
```

## Summary
- flutterfire configure generates platform options.

@lesson flutter-m10-l02 | Firebase Authentication | 8
## Learning objectives
- Sign users in with email and providers

## Firebase Authentication
`firebase_auth` supports email/password, Google, Apple, phone and anonymous sign-in. Listen to `authStateChanges()` to react to login and logout.

```dart
import 'package:firebase_auth/firebase_auth.dart';

Future<UserCredential> signIn(String email, String password) =>
    FirebaseAuth.instance.signInWithEmailAndPassword(email: email, password: password);
```

## Summary
- Drive navigation from authStateChanges().

@lesson flutter-m10-l03 | Firestore | 8
## Learning objectives
- Store and sync documents

## Firestore
Cloud Firestore stores JSON-like documents in collections, syncs in real time and works offline. Use `snapshots()` streams with StreamBuilder.

```dart
import 'package:cloud_firestore/cloud_firestore.dart';

Stream<List<String>> noteTitles(String uid) => FirebaseFirestore.instance
    .collection('users/$uid/notes')
    .orderBy('createdAt', descending: true)
    .snapshots()
    .map((s) => s.docs.map((d) => d['title'] as String).toList());
```

## Summary
- Model data around your queries.

@lesson flutter-m10-l04 | Firebase Storage | 8
## Learning objectives
- Upload and download files

## Firebase Storage
Cloud Storage holds images and files. Upload with `putFile` and save the download URL in Firestore.

```dart
import 'dart:io';
import 'package:firebase_storage/firebase_storage.dart';

Future<String> uploadAvatar(String uid, File file) async {
  final ref = FirebaseStorage.instance.ref('avatars/$uid.jpg');
  await ref.putFile(file);
  return ref.getDownloadURL();
}
```

## Summary
- Store URLs, not files, in Firestore.

@lesson flutter-m10-l05 | Cloud Messaging | 8
## Learning objectives
- Send push notifications

## Cloud Messaging
Firebase Cloud Messaging (FCM) delivers push notifications. Request permission, get the device token, and handle messages in foreground and background.

```dart
import 'package:firebase_messaging/firebase_messaging.dart';

Future<String?> setupPush() async {
  await FirebaseMessaging.instance.requestPermission();
  return FirebaseMessaging.instance.getToken();
}
```

## Summary
- Ask permission before expecting notifications.

@lesson flutter-m10-l06 | Crashlytics | 8
## Learning objectives
- Report crashes from production

## Crashlytics
Crashlytics collects crash reports with stack traces. Forward Flutter and async errors to it.

```dart
import 'package:firebase_crashlytics/firebase_crashlytics.dart';
import 'package:flutter/foundation.dart';

void setupCrashlytics() {
  FlutterError.onError = FirebaseCrashlytics.instance.recordFlutterFatalError;
  PlatformDispatcher.instance.onError = (error, stack) {
    FirebaseCrashlytics.instance.recordError(error, stack, fatal: true);
    return true;
  };
}
```

## Summary
- Catch both framework and async errors.

@lesson flutter-m10-l07 | Analytics | 8
## Learning objectives
- Measure how features are used

## Analytics
Firebase Analytics logs events such as `lesson_completed`. Track a few meaningful events, respect consent, and never log personal data.

```dart
import 'package:firebase_analytics/firebase_analytics.dart';

Future<void> lessonDone(String id) =>
    FirebaseAnalytics.instance.logEvent(name: 'lesson_completed', parameters: {'lesson_id': id});
```

## Summary
- Log meaningful events, no personal data.

@lesson flutter-m10-l08 | Security rules | 8
## Learning objectives
- Protect Firestore and Storage data

## Security rules
Security rules run on Google's servers and decide who can read or write each document. Never ship test-mode rules.

```dart
// firestore.rules
// match /users/{uid}/notes/{noteId} {
//   allow read, write: if request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == uid;
// }
void main() {}
```

## Summary
- Rules, not client code, enforce access.

@lesson flutter-m10-l09 | Firebase integration patterns | 8
## Learning objectives
- Keep Firebase behind repositories

## Firebase integration patterns
Wrap Firebase calls in repository classes so the UI and business logic don't depend on Firebase directly. That makes testing easier and switching backends possible.

```dart
abstract interface class NotesRepository {
  Stream<List<String>> watchTitles(String uid);
  Future<void> add(String uid, String title);
}
```

## Summary
- Depend on interfaces, implement them with Firebase.
